Protocol Target Lab VXLAN software target and client use original MIT project
code and the Python standard library. The accompanying project LICENSE applies.
There is no RTP service dependency or third-party VXLAN runtime stack.

The digest-locked public Python base retains its CPython license at
/usr/local/lib/python3.12/LICENSE.txt and Debian package notices under
/usr/share/doc. Their licenses are not replaced by the wrapper's MIT license.

Original Linux kernel VXLAN/iproute2/capture tools are used only as independent
validation infrastructure in a task-owned namespace. They are not copied into
this runtime or its source asset set. Any redistribution of an oracle tools
image retains its own package/source/license obligations. This image is a
finite ARP VTEP, not a generic kernel L2 carrier or complete OS/source bundle.
